author ai
group gui
note Search, in the GUI. Enter in the search box runs a Rust regex over the lines already in memory - there is no file I/O and no index of its own - and puts the hits into the Model, capped at HIT_LIMIT (five thousand) so a pattern like a single dot cannot freeze the window, with HitsShown recording whether the list was cut so the Search view, its tab and the status all say so, then switches to the Search tab. The tab is drawn by the frame like any other, virtualised so only the visible hits become elements, and clicking one opens that line in the Source view. A re-index drops the hits, since their file and line numbers belong to the old index. The CLI's search and notes commands use the same regex engine.

